=== OBSERVATIONS (backlog, not failures) ===

O-a (carried from BL5.1, now broader): the pinned strings are attribute-ORDER
     and class-list sensitive in all five regions — an equivalent rewrite such as
     `<div role="region" tabindex="0" class="overflow-x-auto" …>` would fail.
     That brittleness is the price of the tabindex guard the ruling asked for;
     noted, not a defect.
O-b (carried from BL5.1, unchanged): the negative clause
     `strings.Contains(html, "text-xs px-2 py-0.5")` is evaluated over the WHOLE
     rendered page, so an unrelated future small-badge on major-expenses would
     trip it spuriously.

